Give JavaScript a way to write to standard output and standard error.

QuickJS has no `console` and componentize-qjs adds none, so what a command
prints is lost. This defines a native `__paneWrite(stream, text)` that
writes to standard output (1) or standard error (2) through the WASI 0.3
libc, which Pane keeps as the package's extension log. Pane's SDK builds
`console` on it (guests/js/console.js) and removes the global.

Modifies componentize-qjs (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE-componentize-qjs); this
patch is distributed under the same license.

